        "Content": "No. 8 Highfield Court enjoys an exceptionally convenient position on Highfield Road in the heart of Rathgar, Dublin 6, one of South Dublin’s most established and sought-after residential locations. The development is set back from the road in mature surroundings, while being only a short stroll from the extensive amenities of Rathgar Village.\r\n\r\nRathgar offers an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, specialist food shops, boutiques and everyday services, with the neighbouring villages of Rathmines, Terenure and Ranelagh also within easy reach. Recreational amenities in the wider area include Palmerston Park and Bushy Park, together with numerous tennis, rugby, hockey and golf clubs.\r\n\r\nThe area is particularly well served by schools, with Rathgar National School, Stratford National School, Zion Parish Primary School and The High School all located nearby, while Terenure College, St Mary’s College, Alexandra College and Gonzaga College are also readily accessible.\r\n\r\nTransport connections are excellent, with frequent bus services along Highfield Road and through Rathgar, together with the LUAS at Cowper and Milltown. Dublin City Centre is approximately 3km away, making Highfield Court an ideal location for those seeking a mature residential setting with excellent access to the city and the wider South Dublin area.\r\n\r\nDescription:\r\nNo. 8 Highfield Court is a well-proportioned one-bedroom apartment extending to approximately 39 sq.m / 420 sq.ft, ideally positioned within this established and mature residential development in the heart of Rathgar, Dublin 6. The property offers bright and practical accommodation throughout and presents an excellent opportunity for a purchaser seeking a home or investment property in one of South Dublin’s most sought-after residential locations.\r\n\r\nThe apartment is accessed via a communal entrance and stairwell, with the accommodation opening into an entrance hallway which provides access to the various rooms. The hallway incorporates two useful storage presses together with a separate hot press, providing valuable additional storage space.\r\n\r\nThe principal living accommodation comprises a bright and generously proportioned living room, providing ample space for both living and dining furniture. A particularly attractive feature of the room is the open fireplace, which provides a traditional focal point and adds character to the main living space. Located off the living area is a separate kitchen, which is compact but functional and provides a good degree of separation from the main reception room.\r\n\r\nThe bedroom is a well-proportioned double room with space for additional bedroom furniture and storage. A separate bathroom completes the internal accommodation.\r\n\r\nHeating is provided by electric storage heaters, while the open fire in the living room provides an additional source of heat. The property is presented in its existing condition and offers an incoming purchaser an excellent opportunity to modernise and upgrade the apartment to their own individual taste and requirements.\r\n\r\nExternally, No. 8 benefits from a car parking space within the development. Highfield Court itself is an established residential development enjoying a mature setting while being exceptionally convenient to the extensive amenities and services available throughout Rathgar and the surrounding Dublin 6 area.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 39 sq.m / 420 sq.ft, No. 8 Highfield Court combines a highly desirable location with well-balanced accommodation and excellent potential. The property is likely to appeal to first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike, particularly those looking to acquire a property within easy reach of Rathgar Village and Dublin City Centre."
      },
